How to setup a new Robot 

1. Install Ubuntu 22.04
    a. Create a user
        username: dev
        password: panda


2. Manual Configuration
    a. Give it wireless wifi access
        Can be as easy as connection to WIFI@OSU

    b. Bring things up to date
        sudo apt update
        sudo apt upgrade

    c. Install networking tools onto the panda
        sudo apt install net-tools
        sudo apt install ifmetric

    d. Configure the panda to prefer the wireless network over the ethernet
        sudo nmcli connection modify 'Wired connection 1' ipv4.route-metric 5000
            you may need to replace the name Wired connection 1; (nmclid device) gets names
        sudo nmcli connection up
        Verify by running "route -n" (lower metric == more preferred)
    
    e. Ensure there is a running ssh server on the panda
        sudo apt install openssh-server
        sudo service ssh restart

    f. Get the panda MAC Address (Write this down for later)
        ip addr show
        Write Down the ethernet and wireless addresses (look something like ##:##:##:##:##:##)
            ethernet is under en****
            wireless is under wl****

    g. Setup passwordless sudo
        sudo visudo
        add "dev ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL" to the end and save


3. AMR Net Configuration
    a. Wire peer to peer connection to dev laptop
        Plug both dev laptop and panda into router (not the yellow port)

    b. Ensure the reserves the panda's id
        On the dev laptop go to the rotuer's ip in a web browser (typically 192.168.1.1) - you need to click on the screen to get to the settings page
        Log into the router (Router password = admin)
        Go to Connectivity->Local Network->DHCP Reservations
        Manually add device reservation
            DeviceName: Robot#Wired
            Assign IP Address: 192.168.1.20#
            To: MAC Address: {MAC Address you wrote down earlier: ethernet}
        Save
        Manually add device reservation
            DeviceName: Robot#Wireless
            Assign IP Address: 192.168.1.22#
            To: MAC Address: {MAC Address you wrote down earlier: wireless}
        Save

    c. Set Static DCHP on panda
        Settings->Network->Wired Setting Icon->IPV4->Manual
            Address: 192.168.1.20#
            Netmask: 255.255.255.0
        Apply

    d. Reboot panda 
        Verify the panda now has the correct ip (ip addr)

    e. Add Hostname on Dev Computer
        edit /etc/hosts
        add "192.168.1.20#  Robot#Wired" to the file and save
        add "192.168.1.22#  Robot#Wireless" to the file and save


4. Install Many Many Things onto the device